[bug]		hounan
	The relay-port RAI sub-option (code 19), defined in
	RFC 8357, is a zero-length sub-option. Kea used to
	define it as uint16, which caused kea-dhcp4 to drop
	relayed packets carrying a compliant "19 00"
	sub-option with an "OptionInt 19 truncated" error.
	The definition is now "empty" and such packets are
	processed correctly.
	(Gitlab #4846)
